                        "entry_id": "ea62be07-39ea-388c-9449-34ffd24b509d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The wake, or watching, held over a corpse before burial."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "32d8d871-0037-4665-afdc-bef81d28c372",
                                "sense_id": "d78af1a6-6617-3d59-82ab-d5d64c30b1b7",
                                "text": "In some parts of Scotland is still kept up the custon of Lyke-wake (Lich-wake), or watching beside the dead body before its burial."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3752d4a-42b3-4573-ae99-abedfcec36bc",
                                "sense_id": "d78af1a6-6617-3d59-82ab-d5d64c30b1b7",
                                "text": "Funeral rites in the house (lich wakes) should be avoided out of regard for the health of the members of the family."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a9ab94f-3e8c-4f45-a7ee-f54426d3a32f",
                                "sense_id": "d78af1a6-6617-3d59-82ab-d5d64c30b1b7",
                                "text": "The custom of the \"lich-wake,\" corresponding largely with the surviving Irish custom of waking the dead, had not then died out in Scotland, and in Monifieth was frequently practised."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
